                        "form": "rupicaprines"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2775a349-8133-3d43-a0e2-1d0453be3538",
                        "entry_id": "d5b78313-5603-339f-bb58-0340060d37fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A mammal of the genus Rupicapra; a chamois."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5af8acac-37eb-45cc-8b32-dd426a090938",
                                "sense_id": "2775a349-8133-3d43-a0e2-1d0453be3538",
                                "text": "An excellent indication of this fact is the absence in Pityusic Pleistocene sites of the rupicaprine Myotragus, which is so frequent in the ossiferous Quaternary breccia of Mallorca and Menorca."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7781be58-ce7d-4856-9655-08268b9af08d",
                                "sense_id": "2775a349-8133-3d43-a0e2-1d0453be3538",
                                "text": "The caprines, apart from rupicaprines and Saigini have been included by Schaller (1977) in the category 'selective grazer and browser; uses several vegetation types; seasonal diet change; large home area' of Jarman's (1974) classification."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9376d8e5-0704-436b-ba19-91c41b650426",
                                "sense_id": "2775a349-8133-3d43-a0e2-1d0453be3538",
                                "text": "These two very distinct genera appear to form a convenient bridge between the antelopes on the one hand and the rupicaprines on the other."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
